{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"Voygr POI API","description":"Validate and enrich place data. Make business phone calls with PlaceCall.\n\n\nPlaceCall is the API for outbound phone calls executed by an AI voice agent.\nSubmit a task, then retrieve the structured outcome and transcript.\n\n## Authentication\n\nSend `X-API-Key` with every request. Keys carry a credit balance and usage limits.\n\n## Placing a call\n\n`POST /calls` accepts two shapes. Freeform uses `target_phone` and `brief`:\n\n```json\n{\"target_phone\": \"+15551234567\", \"brief\": \"Ask when the kitchen closes tonight.\", \"language\": \"en\"}\n```\n\nStructured calls use `intent` and `slots`:\n\n| Intent | Required slots |\n|---|---|\n| `inquiry` | `target_phone`, `question` |\n| `info_gathering` | `target_phone`, `questions` |\n| `issue_resolution` | `target_phone`, `issue_description` |\n| `booking` | `target_phone`, `name`, `date`, `time`, `party_size` |\n| `cancellation` | `booking_id` (uses the stored booking's phone) |\n\nAn incomplete submission returns `422` listing missing slots with a\n`suggested_question`: collect answers and resubmit. Validation does not dial or\ncharge. A balance that cannot cover the hold returns `402` even for an incomplete\nsubmission. `language` accepts `en`, `es`, `fr`, `de`, `hi`, `ru`, `pt`, `ja`, `it`,\n`nl`, `sr`, `tr`, `pl`, or `auto` (default); other codes return\n`422 unsupported_language`.\n\nFor `201`, freeform returns a `call` wrapper and structured returns the flat\n`SkillRunResponse`. A call accepted for later dialing returns `202`: freeform\nuses `QueuedCallResponse`, structured uses `SkillRunResponse` with `status=queued`.\nPoll `GET /calls/{call_id}` for either shape.\n\n## Call lifecycle\n\nCalls are asynchronous. Poll until `status` is `completed`, `failed`, or\n`cancelled`; then read `outcome_type`, `outcome_summary`, and `transcript_full`.\nThere is no completion webhook. Stream `GET /calls/{call_id}/events?after_event_id=0`\nand process each SSE event as it arrives. Ignore heartbeat events and comments,\nkeeping the last event ID when a heartbeat has no `id`. On a\ndisconnect while the call is active, reconnect with `after_event_id` set to the\nlast `id:` received; use that query cursor rather than `Last-Event-ID`.\nChoose `ask_user_mode: \"stream\"` to receive `ask_user` events and answer through\n`POST /calls/{call_id}/answer`. Cancel through `POST /calls/{call_id}/cancel`.\n\n`GET /calls/{call_id}/transcript-merged` provides a fuller post-call transcript\nincluding phone menus and hold announcements; `transcript_full` remains the\ncurrent conversation transcript. `202 {\"status\": \"merger_pending\"}` means it is\nnot available yet, not a guarantee it will become available. Retry after the\n`transcript_ready` event or poll the GET. For a persistent `202`, request one\n`POST /calls/{call_id}/transcript-merged/rebuild`. Do not poll the rebuild endpoint.\n\n## Billing\n\nA call requires 30 credits available for a refundable hold. Successful outcomes cost 10 credits; unsuccessful outcomes cost 0. At completion the hold is released and only the settled amount is charged.\n\n`credits_reserved` is 0 for calls through api.voygr.tech, whether they start\nimmediately or are queued; zero does not mean no balance is held. It is not the final charge.\nRead `credits_charge_on_success` for the successful-outcome charge. Insufficient\navailable balance returns `402`. `GET /v1/usage` reports `available` and\n`call_credit_hold`; `available // call_credit_hold` is the credit-limited call\ncount, subject to other limits.\n\n## Limits\n\nLimits depend on your key; handle 429 responses and retry guidance.\nConcurrent-call limits return `409` with `active_call_ids`. Maintenance returns\n`503` with `resume_at`.\n\n## Acceptable use\n\nCalls are transactional and user-initiated only: no telemarketing,\nsolicitation, bulk dialing, or harassment. The agent discloses that it is an\nAI assistant and that the call is recorded; disclosure is not configurable.\nUnited States destinations only. Recordings and transcripts are retained for\na maximum of 90 days.\n\n\nCredit rates: validation and enrichment are 1 credit per request. A PlaceCall call is 10 credits, charged only when the call reaches a real conversation. Credits never expire.","version":"1.0.0"},"paths":{"/v1/validate":{"post":{"tags":["core"],"summary":"Validate a place","description":"Validate a place's existence and operating status using evidence about the place.","operationId":"validate_poi_v1_validate_post","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/POIValidateRequest"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/POIValidateResponse"}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request. Correct the fields before retrying.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","const":false},"error":{"type":"string"},"error_code":{"type":"string","const":"VALIDATION_ERROR"},"request_id":{"type":["string","null"]},"validation_timestamp":{"type":"string"},"detail":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"field":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"}},"required":["field","message","type"]}}},"required":["success","error","error_code","request_id","validation_timestamp","detail"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"detail":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"},"error_code":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"],"description":"Gateway rejection, for example an invalid Idempotency-Key header."}},"required":["detail"]}]},"examples":{"invalid_input":{"value":{"success":false,"error":"Invalid input provided","error_code":"VALIDATION_ERROR","request_id":"example-request-id","validation_timestamp":"2026-09-16T12:00:00Z","detail":[{"field":"poi_name","message":"Field required","type":"missing"}]}}}}}}}}},"/v1/enrich":{"post":{"tags":["core"],"summary":"Enrich a place","description":"Return requested attributes for one place or a list of places. Standard attributes (opening_hours, phone, website, facebook, instagram, tiktok, email, existence, open_closed) cost one credit per place however many you request; any other attribute name is a research field, answered by a bounded research loop and charged per place per field. A request may mix both and pays for each. Send poi_name for one place and get the flat response; send pois for a list and get a rows-by-attributes matrix. include_summary=true also returns a short factual place_summary. Requires a key with the enrich or deep_research entitlement; either one may request any attribute, standard or custom. See [Research custom attributes](/docs/guides/research-custom-attributes/) for custom attributes.\n\n### Verifying the name and address you sent\n\nWhen your records may be close but not exact - an abbreviation, an initialism, a\nstore number, or a slightly stale spelling - three independent checks are\navailable, one for each thing a record can get wrong:\n\n- `verify_name` settles what the business is actually called BEFORE researching\n  anything else, and every attribute you asked for is then researched against\n  the verified name. Each row carries `identity.name`.\n- `verify_address` checks the trading address AFTER research and never replaces\n  it. Each row carries `address_checks.address`.\n- `verify_registered_address` checks the registered office. Each row carries\n  `address_checks.registered_address`.\n\n`identity.name` gives the value we settled on, a verdict, and your original. The\nverdict is `confirmed` (yours was already right), `corrected` (we replaced it) or\n`unresolved` (we could not establish it, so your value comes back untouched).\n`value` is always what the rest of the row was researched against, so branch on\nthe verdict rather than comparing strings.\n\nFormatting is not a correction: punctuation, casing, \"and\" vs \"&\" and a dropped\nor added Inc/Ltd/LLC all come back `confirmed` with your own string.\n\n`verify_name` and `verify_address` share one lookup, so either or both cost a flat\n1 extra credit per row, independent of how many attributes you requested;\n`verify_registered_address` costs 1 more. Each can be overridden per place.\n\n`verify_identity` is deprecated. It means `verify_name` plus `verify_address`,\ncosts the same 1, and additionally rewrites the address research runs against to\nthe same premises written in full - never a different one - returning\n`identity.address` too. Use the separate flags in new integrations, so a place can\ndecline either check on its own.\n\nThis is not a postal validation - a `confirmed` address matches what the business\npublishes about itself, not a postal database - and it makes no claim about\nwhether the business is still open.\n\n\n### Owner discovery (`owners`, `owner_org`)\n\n`owners` is the individual owner, co-owners or franchisee, as one value: a list\nof people with a `name` and a `role`. Add `include` (`phone`, `email`,\n`linkedin`) to look up each owner's direct contacts, returned in the same\nobjects. `owner_org` is the operating company when no individual owner exists.\nThey are mutually exclusive per place: when one is established, the other\nabstains. \"no individual owner\" is a legitimate answer. `key_people` takes the\nsame shape with `title` in place of `role`.\n\n`owners` and `key_people` carry no confidence score. Unavailable ownership is a\nnormal result; do not interpret an abstention as a claim that no owner exists.\n`owners` and `key_people` cost 1 credit for the names, 1 for the roles or\ntitles and 1 per included contact; `owner_org` is billed like any other field.\nSee [Owners and key people](/docs/guides/owners-and-key-people/).\n","operationId":"enrich_poi_v1_enrich_post","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UnifiedEnrichRequest"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/POIEnrichResponse"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DeepResearchResponse"}],"title":"Response Enrich Poi V1 Enrich Post"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"402":{"description":"Not enough credits, or the estimate exceeds the caller's ceiling.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"quota_exceeded":{"summary":"Insufficient available credits","value":{"detail":{"error":"quota_exceeded","needed_credits":120,"checkout_url":"/checkout/buy"}}},"max_credits_exceeded":{"summary":"Up-front estimate exceeds request max_credits (nothing charged)","value":{"detail":{"success":false,"error":"max_credits_exceeded","detail":"Estimated cost 120 credits exceeds max_credits 100; nothing was run or charged.","estimated_credits":120}}}}}}},"403":{"description":"This key is not permitted to use this endpoint. It needs the enrich or deep_research entitlement.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"not_entitled":{"value":{"detail":{"error":"endpoint not permitted for this key"}}}}}}},"422":{"description":"Coordinates could not be resolved to a location. Correct the coordinates or send an address.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","const":false},"error":{"type":"string"},"error_code":{"type":"string","const":"VALIDATION_ERROR"},"request_id":{"type":["string","null"]},"validation_timestamp":{"type":"string"}},"required":["success","error","error_code","request_id","validation_timestamp"]},"examples":{"unresolved_coordinates":{"value":{"success":false,"error":"Could not resolve the given coordinates to a location.","error_code":"VALIDATION_ERROR","request_id":"example-request-id","validation_timestamp":"2026-09-16T12:00:00Z"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request. Correct the fields before retrying.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","const":false},"error":{"type":"string"},"error_code":{"type":"string","const":"VALIDATION_ERROR"},"request_id":{"type":["string","null"]},"validation_timestamp":{"type":"string"},"detail":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"field":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"}},"required":["field","message","type"]}}},"required":["success","error","error_code","request_id","validation_timestamp","detail"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"detail":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"},"error_code":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"],"description":"Gateway rejection, for example an invalid Idempotency-Key header."}},"required":["detail"]}]},"examples":{"invalid_input":{"value":{"success":false,"error":"Invalid input provided","error_code":"VALIDATION_ERROR","request_id":"example-request-id","validation_timestamp":"2026-09-16T12:00:00Z","detail":[{"field":"poi_name","message":"Field required","type":"missing"}]}}}}}}}}},"/v1/usage":{"get":{"tags":["core"],"summary":"View API usage","description":"Get current usage, quota, and reset date for the API key.","operationId":"get_usage_v1_usage_get","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UsageResponse"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing API key header","content":{"application/json":{"example":{"success":false,"error":"API key required. Include X-API-Key header.","error_code":"AUTHENTICATION_ERROR","request_id":"ad33009a-fdfe-4e25-9650-4a49099c3d4a"},"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"}}}},"403":{"description":"Invalid, revoked, or unauthorized API key","content":{"application/json":{"example":{"success":false,"error":"Invalid or revoked API key","error_code":"AUTHENTICATION_ERROR","request_id":"25b104f0-9ad0-4fc7-8530-c5d5ff8d9698"},"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/v1/jobs/validate":{"post":{"tags":["core"],"summary":"Validate places in bulk","operationId":"create_jobs_validate_v1_jobs_validate_post","parameters":[{"name":"Idempotency-Key","in":"header","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Idempotency-Key"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ValidateJobSubmit"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ValidationJobSubmitResponse"}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request. Correct the fields before retrying.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","const":false},"error":{"type":"string"},"error_code":{"type":"string","const":"VALIDATION_ERROR"},"request_id":{"type":["string","null"]},"validation_timestamp":{"type":"string"},"detail":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"field":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"}},"required":["field","message","type"]}}},"required":["success","error","error_code","request_id","validation_timestamp","detail"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"detail":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"},"error_code":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"],"description":"Gateway rejection, for example an invalid Idempotency-Key header."}},"required":["detail"]}]},"examples":{"invalid_input":{"value":{"success":false,"error":"Invalid input provided","error_code":"VALIDATION_ERROR","request_id":"example-request-id","validation_timestamp":"2026-09-16T12:00:00Z","detail":[{"field":"pois.0.poi_name","message":"Field required","type":"missing"}]}}}}}}},"description":"Submit 1 to 10,000 places for asynchronous validation. Each downloaded JSON Lines row follows the POST /v1/validate response contract. Save batch_id and poll GET /v1/jobs/{batch_id} after acceptance. For an uncertain submission, retry promptly with the same Idempotency-Key and identical body. Replay only applies while the idempotency record is retained and the job is not cancelled. Reusing a key after cancellation or retention expiry can create new work and charges. While replay applies, a different body returns 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT. Use a new key for intentional new work."}},"/v1/jobs/enrich":{"post":{"tags":["core"],"summary":"Enrich places in bulk","description":"Enrich up to 10,000 places asynchronously using /v1/enrich request bodies. Poll GET /v1/jobs/{batch_id} until completed, then download result.jsonl.gz: one result per input row, in order. One credit per row is held at submission; only rows with a billable value or non-null status are charged, and unused credits are released. Failed rows are free. Save batch_id and poll GET /v1/jobs/{batch_id} after acceptance. For an uncertain submission, retry promptly with the same Idempotency-Key and identical body. Replay only applies while the idempotency record is retained and the job is not cancelled. Reusing a key after cancellation or retention expiry can create new work and charges. While replay applies, a different body returns 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT. Use a new key for intentional new work.","operationId":"create_jobs_enrich_v1_jobs_enrich_post","parameters":[{"name":"Idempotency-Key","in":"header","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Idempotency-Key"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EnrichJobSubmit"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ValidationJobSubmitResponse"}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request. Correct the fields before retrying.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","const":false},"error":{"type":"string"},"error_code":{"type":"string","const":"VALIDATION_ERROR"},"request_id":{"type":["string","null"]},"validation_timestamp":{"type":"string"},"detail":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"field":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"}},"required":["field","message","type"]}}},"required":["success","error","error_code","request_id","validation_timestamp","detail"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"detail":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"},"error_code":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"],"description":"Gateway rejection, for example an invalid Idempotency-Key header."}},"required":["detail"]}]},"examples":{"invalid_input":{"value":{"success":false,"error":"Invalid input provided","error_code":"VALIDATION_ERROR","request_id":"example-request-id","validation_timestamp":"2026-09-16T12:00:00Z","detail":[{"field":"pois.0.poi_name","message":"Field required","type":"missing"}]}}}}}}}}},"/v1/jobs/{batch_id}":{"get":{"tags":["core"],"summary":"Get batch job status and results","description":"Status, progress and ETA for a submitted job. When `status` is `completed`, the response carries `results.files[]` with a presigned download URL (expires in ~15 minutes - poll again for a fresh one). The file is gzipped JSONL: one result line per input row, in input order.","operationId":"get_validation_job_v1_jobs__batch_id__get","parameters":[{"name":"batch_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Batch Id"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ValidationJobStatus"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}},"delete":{"tags":["core"],"summary":"Cancel a batch job","description":"Request cancellation of a queued or running job (any type). Rows already processed are kept, billed, and downloadable; unprocessed rows are not charged.","operationId":"delete_validation_job_v1_jobs__batch_id__delete","parameters":[{"name":"batch_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Batch Id"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ValidationJobDeleteResponse"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/calls":{"post":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Place a call","description":"Place an outbound AI phone call. Two request shapes - freeform (target_phone + brief) or structured (target_phone + intent + slots). See the guide above for the 422 slot-retry loop.","operationId":"create_call","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CallCreateRequest"},"examples":{"freeform":{"summary":"Freeform brief","value":{"target_phone":"+15551234567","brief":"Call and ask what time the kitchen closes tonight. Thank them and hang up.","language":"en"}},"structured":{"summary":"Structured slots","value":{"target_phone":"+15551234567","intent":"inquiry","slots":{"intent":"inquiry","target_phone":"+15551234567","question":"What time does the kitchen close tonight?"}}}}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Call created. The envelope shape depends on which request path was used - freeform returns CallResponse (a `call` wrapper), structured returns the flat SkillRunResponse (top-level call_id, no wrapper). Either way, poll GET /calls/{call_id} afterward - that response is identical regardless of which path created the call.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CallResponse"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SkillRunResponse"}]},"examples":{"freeform_response":{"summary":"Freeform path -> CallResponse (call wrapper)","value":{"call":{"call_id":"c_abc123","customer_id":"cus_xyz","target_phone":"+15551234567","language":"en","status":"dialing","started_at":null,"ended_at":null,"duration_sec":null,"outcome_type":null,"outcome_summary":null,"outcome_charge_cents":0,"created_at":"2026-07-17T12:00:00Z","has_recording":false,"recording_url":null,"reservation_signals":null,"transcript_full":null},"credits_reserved":0,"credits_charge_on_success":10}},"structured_response":{"summary":"Structured path -> SkillRunResponse (flat, no wrapper)","value":{"call_id":"c_abc123","status":"dialing","credits_reserved":0,"credits_charge_on_success":10,"status_url":"/calls/c_abc123","answer_url":"/calls/c_abc123/answer","recording_url":"/calls/c_abc123/recording","replayed":false,"expected_next_steps":["..."]}}}}}},"202":{"description":"Call accepted for later dialing. Freeform returns QueuedCallResponse; structured returns SkillRunResponse with status=queued. Poll GET /calls/{call_id} for progress.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/QueuedCallResponse"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SkillRunResponse"}]},"examples":{"freeform_queued":{"summary":"Freeform path, queued -> QueuedCallResponse","value":{"call_id":"c_abc123","position":0,"status":"queued"}},"structured_queued":{"summary":"Structured queued response; credits_reserved=0 does not mean no balance is held","value":{"call_id":"c_abc123","status":"queued","credits_reserved":0,"status_url":"/calls/c_abc123","answer_url":"/calls/c_abc123/answer","recording_url":"/calls/c_abc123/recording","replayed":false,"expected_next_steps":["..."]}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"402":{"description":"Insufficient credits for the 30-credit refundable hold.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"quota_exceeded":{"summary":"Insufficient available credits","value":{"detail":{"error":"quota_exceeded","needed_credits":30,"checkout_url":"/checkout/buy"}}}}}}},"403":{"description":"Key not permitted to make this request.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"tier_not_permitted":{"value":{"detail":{"error":"tier not permitted"}}},"missing_entitlement":{"value":{"detail":{"error":"missing entitlement: booking"}}},"freeform_disabled":{"summary":"Freeform brief disabled for this key","value":{"detail":{"error_code":"freeform_disabled","hint":"Submit structured `slots` (see GET /skills) or ask ops to enable freeform for this key."}}}}}}},"409":{"description":"Concurrent-call cap reached.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"concurrent_call_not_allowed":{"value":{"detail":{"error":"concurrent_call_not_allowed","max_concurrent":2,"active_call_ids":["c_abc123"]}}}}}}},"422":{"description":"Bad request body - four flavors, distinguished by error_code, plus standard Pydantic validation.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_brief":{"summary":"Freeform path, brief absent/empty","value":{"detail":{"error_code":"missing_brief","hint":"Provide `brief` (freeform) or `slots` (structured) - see GET /skills/concierge/manifest."}}},"missing_slots":{"summary":"Structured path, required slots absent (flagship retry loop)","value":{"detail":{"error_code":"missing_slots","slot_schema_version":"concierge-v1","intent_type":"inquiry","missing_slots":[{"slot_name":"question","reason":"the single question the agent must ask the venue","suggested_question":"What should we ask them?","type_hint":"free_text"}],"invalid":{},"hint":"Collect the listed slots from your user and resubmit with `slots` populated."}}},"unknown_intent":{"summary":"intent not a supported value","value":{"detail":{"error_code":"unknown_intent","slot_schema_version":"concierge-v1","supported_intents":["booking","cancellation","info_gathering","inquiry","issue_resolution"],"hint":"Pick a supported intent and resubmit."}}},"invalid_slots":{"summary":"A free-text slot exceeds 2000 characters","value":{"detail":{"error_code":"invalid_slots","slot_schema_version":"concierge-v1","invalid":{"question":"must be at most 2000 characters"},"hint":"Shorten the listed free-text slots to at most 2000 characters and resubmit."}}},"pydantic_validation":{"summary":"Standard field validation, e.g. missing target_phone","value":{"detail":[{"type":"missing","loc":["body","target_phone"],"msg":"Field required","input":{"intent":"inquiry","slots":{"intent":"inquiry"}}}]}}}}}},"429":{"description":"Limits depend on your key; handle 429 responses and retry guidance.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"rate_limited":{"value":{"detail":{"error":"rate limit exceeded"}}}}}}},"503":{"description":"Service in a maintenance window.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"maintenance":{"value":{"detail":{"error":"maintenance","message":"...","resume_at":"2026-07-17T13:00:00Z"}}}}}}}}},"get":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"List calls","description":"List your own calls, most recent first. Each entry omits transcript_full; fetch a single call for the transcript.","operationId":"list_calls","parameters":[{"name":"limit","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","default":100,"minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"title":"Limit"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CallDTO"}}}}},"400":{"description":"limit outside 1..1000.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"bad_limit":{"value":{"detail":"limit must be between 1 and 1000"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}}}}},"/calls/{call_id}":{"get":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Get a call","description":"Poll a single call. Returns the full detail fields (including transcript_full) that the list endpoint omits.","operationId":"get_call","parameters":[{"name":"call_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Call Id"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CallDTO"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Call not found, or isn't yours.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"not_found":{"value":{"detail":"Call not found"}}}}}}}}},"/calls/{call_id}/answer":{"post":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Answer a mid-call question","description":"Answer a question the agent asked mid-call. If no answer arrives before the wait window elapses, the call proceeds and wraps up gracefully rather than stalling indefinitely.","operationId":"answer_call","parameters":[{"name":"call_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Call Id"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AnswerRequest"},"examples":{"answer":{"value":{"answer":"Yes, hold the table until 7:30pm"}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AnswerResponse"},"examples":{"delivered":{"value":{"delivered":true,"reason":"delivered"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}}}}},"/calls/{call_id}/events":{"get":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Poll call events (SSE-formatted)","description":"Stream live call events as text/event-stream, parsing each SSE event as it arrives rather than waiting for the response to finish. Use after_event_id=0 initially; on reconnect, pass the last received id as after_event_id. Last-Event-ID is not supported. Heartbeat events keep idle connections alive; ignore them and SSE comments, preserving the last event ID when no id is present. Reconnect after a disconnect while the call is active, and check GET /calls/{call_id} for its terminal status. Events include status_change, ask_user, outcome, recording_ready, transcript_ready. Set ask_user_mode=stream when creating a call and answer ask_user promptly via POST /calls/{call_id}/answer.","operationId":"get_call_events","parameters":[{"name":"call_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Call Id"}},{"name":"after_event_id","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"title":"After Event Id"},"description":"Return only events with event_id greater than this cursor. Start at 0; advance to the last `id:` you received."}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"SSE-formatted text; empty body when no new events.","content":{"text/event-stream":{"schema":{"type":"string"},"examples":{"status_change":{"value":"id: 2077\nevent: status_change\ndata: {\"event_id\": 2077, \"call_id\": \"c_abc123\", \"event_type\": \"status_change\", \"data\": {\"status\": \"dialing\"}}\n\n"}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Call not found, or isn't yours.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"not_found":{"value":{"detail":"Call not found"}}}}}}}}},"/calls/{call_id}/transcript-merged":{"get":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Get the post-call merged transcript","description":"The post-call merged transcript contains both sides of the call on one timeline. It can include speech absent from the current transcript_full, such as phone menus and hold announcements. Read it after the call ends.","operationId":"get_transcript_merged","parameters":[{"name":"call_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Call Id"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MergedTranscript"},"examples":{"merged":{"value":{"version":1,"duration_ms":17240,"turns":[{"speaker":"hostess","start_ms":300,"end_ms":6100,"text":"Thank you for calling. If you know your party's extension, you may dial it at any time."},{"speaker":"bot","start_ms":6800,"end_ms":9200,"text":"Hi, this is an AI assistant calling to ask about your opening hours."}]}}}}}},"202":{"description":"Merged transcript not yet available. Retry after transcript_ready, or poll this GET. A 202 is not a guarantee it will become available: if it persists after the call ends, request one rebuild with POST /calls/{call_id}/transcript-merged/rebuild.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"merger_pending":{"value":{"status":"merger_pending"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Call not found or isn't yours - also returned for calls where the callee declined recording (no verbatim transcript may be served; the summary + outcome on GET /calls/{call_id} remain available).","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"not_found":{"value":{"detail":"Transcript not available"}}}}}}}}},"/calls/{call_id}/transcript-merged/rebuild":{"post":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Rebuild the merged transcript now","description":"Rebuild and return a past call's merged transcript from its recording. Use for missing or stale transcripts, including a persistent 202 from GET. Idempotent: replaces the stored transcript. Do not poll with rebuild; poll the GET or wait for transcript_ready.","operationId":"rebuild_transcript_merged","parameters":[{"name":"call_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Call Id"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The rebuilt transcript - same body as the GET.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MergedTranscript"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Call not found or isn't yours - also returned for calls where the callee declined recording (no verbatim transcript may be served).","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"not_found":{"value":{"detail":"Transcript not available"}}}}}},"425":{"description":"The recording isn't available yet - the call may still be finalizing. Nothing failed; retry shortly. On an old call, though, a persistent 425 means the recording no longer exists (retention purge) and the transcript cannot be rebuilt.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"recording_pending":{"value":{"status":"recording_pending"}}}}}},"503":{"description":"The rebuild hit a dependency failure. Safe to retry.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"merge_failed":{"value":{"status":"merge_failed"}}}}}},"504":{"description":"The request timed out, but the transcript may still become available. Recover it with GET /calls/{call_id}/transcript-merged before requesting another rebuild.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"backend_timeout":{"value":{"error":"backend timeout","error_code":"BACKEND_TIMEOUT"}}}}}}}}},"/calls/{call_id}/cancel":{"post":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Cancel a queued or active call","description":"Best-effort cancel. Returns `{\"cancelled\": true}` when the call was still cancellable (queued/dialing), `{\"cancelled\": false}` when it already reached a terminal state - safe to call idempotently.","operationId":"cancel_call","parameters":[{"name":"call_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Call Id"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"cancelled":{"type":"boolean","title":"Cancelled"}},"required":["cancelled"]},"examples":{"already_terminal":{"value":{"cancelled":false}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Call not found, or isn't yours.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"not_found":{"value":{"detail":"Call not found"}}}}}}}}},"/skills":{"get":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"List available skills","description":"Discovery for the structured path: every runnable skill with its manifest/run URLs. The concierge skill owns the three POST /calls structured intents.","operationId":"list_skills","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"skill_id":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string"},"description":{"type":"string"},"manifest_url":{"type":"string"},"run_url":{"type":"string"}},"required":["skill_id","title","manifest_url"]}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}}}}},"/skills/{skill_id}/manifest":{"get":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Get a skill's manifest (slot schemas)","description":"Machine-readable contract for a skill: `input_schema` (JSON Schema for its slots), `intent_types_supported`, `event_types`, `ask_user_modes_supported`, URL templates and limits. The 422 `missing_slots` hints on POST /calls point here - fetch it once and drive slot collection from it.","operationId":"get_skill_manifest","parameters":[{"name":"skill_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Skill Id","examples":["concierge"]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"description":"Keys include: skill_id, title, description, version, input_schema, intent_types_supported, event_types, ask_user_modes_supported, run/status/answer/events URL templates, limits."}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Unknown skill_id.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"not_found":{"value":{"detail":"Skill not found"}}}}}}}}},"/users/me":{"get":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Who am I / quota snapshot","description":"Identity + quota for the presented API key. Lighter-weight companion to GET /v1/usage with key metadata included.","operationId":"get_me","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"api_key_id":{"type":"string"},"customer_id":{"type":"string"},"customer_name":{"type":"string"},"api_key_last_4":{"type":"string"},"status":{"type":"string"},"quota_limit":{"type":"integer"},"current_usage":{"type":"integer"},"quota_period":{"type":"string"},"ask_user_webhook_url":{"type":["string","null"]},"ask_user_webhook_configured":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["api_key_id","customer_id","quota_limit","current_usage"]}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}}}}},"/users/me/webhook":{"put":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Register the webhook for mid-call questions","description":"Register the HTTPS endpoint we POST to when the agent needs an answer from you DURING a call - a hostess asking for a callback number, an IVR wanting a choice. Without one, those questions arrive only on GET /calls/{call_id}/events, which means holding a stream open for each call. The same question always goes to both channels carrying the same request_id; answer either, and deduplicate on that id. Reply 200 with an answer field to answer inline, or 202 and then POST /calls/{call_id}/answer when you have it. One 60-second budget covers the POST and the wait after it - the callee is on hold for all of it.","operationId":"set_webhook","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SetWebhookRequest"},"examples":{"register":{"summary":"Register and issue a secret","value":{"url":"https://hooks.example.com/callwright"}},"change_url_only":{"summary":"Point at a new URL, keep the secret","value":{"url":"https://hooks.example.com/v2","regenerate_secret":false}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Registered. The secret is present only when this request issued one, and is shown ONCE.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SetWebhookResponse"},"examples":{"issued":{"value":{"url":"https://hooks.example.com/callwright","secret":"q3Jv8kX0bF5yW2mN7tL1cR9eHs4dZa6pU0iOgVnYxEw"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The URL is not a permitted destination - not HTTPS, carries credentials, or resolves to a private or reserved address. Nothing was stored.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"not_https":{"value":{"detail":"Only HTTPS webhook URLs are accepted"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"422":{"description":"Body failed validation (e.g. url is absent or not a URL).","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_url":{"value":{"detail":[{"type":"missing","loc":["body","url"],"msg":"Field required"}]}}}}}}}},"delete":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Remove the webhook","description":"Remove the registered URL and its secret. Mid-call questions then arrive only on GET /calls/{call_id}/events. Afterwards ask_user_webhook_url and ask_user_webhook_configured on GET /users/me read back as null and false. Clearing a webhook that was not set is not an error.","operationId":"clear_webhook","responses":{"200":{"description":"Cleared.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ClearWebhookResponse"},"examples":{"cleared":{"value":{"cleared":true}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}}}}},"/users/me/limits":{"put":{"tags":["calls"],"summary":"Set the concurrent-call limit","description":"Raise (or lower) how many calls this key may have in flight at once. Use this to recover from a 409 concurrent_call_not_allowed: read your ceiling from max_concurrent_calls_ceiling on GET /users/me, then PUT a value up to it. A value above the ceiling is refused with 403 (nothing is changed). A new key starts at 1, so raise it here when you need parallel dialing.","operationId":"set_limits","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SetLimitsRequest"},"examples":{"raise_to_ceiling":{"summary":"Raise the in-flight cap to 1","value":{"max_concurrent_calls":1}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The new limit, echoed with the ceiling it was checked against.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/LimitsResponse"},"examples":{"set":{"value":{"max_concurrent_calls":1,"max_concurrent_calls_ceiling":1}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing or invalid X-API-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"missing_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key header absent","value":{"detail":{"error":"API key required"}}},"invalid_key":{"summary":"X-API-Key doesn't resolve to an active key","value":{"detail":{"error":"invalid API key"}}}}}}},"403":{"description":"Requested value exceeds the admin-set ceiling on this key - nothing was changed.","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"ceiling_exceeded":{"value":{"detail":{"error":"max_concurrent_calls_ceiling_exceeded","requested":5,"max_allowed":1}}}}}}},"422":{"description":"Body failed validation (e.g. max_concurrent_calls below 1, or above the service hard maximum).","content":{"application/json":{"examples":{"too_low":{"value":{"detail":[{"type":"greater_than_equal","loc":["body","max_concurrent_calls"],"msg":"Input should be greater than or equal to 1"}]}}}}}}}}},"/v1/pricing":{"get":{"tags":["core"],"summary":"Get the public credit rate card","description":"What a call, a place lookup and a single-record validation cost, in credits, read from the gateway's own pricing. No key needed: quote a job before you spend. `operator_owned: true` marks a rate the operator sets outside this API - show it as current, not as a promise. Packs are at `/checkout/packs`; rates that depend on your key are on `GET /v1/usage`.","operationId":"get_pricing_v1_pricing_get","responses":{"200":{"description":"The rate card. Cacheable for five minutes.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PricingCard"}}}}},"security":[]}}},"components":{"schemas":{"AddressCheck":{"properties":{"address_source":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["provided","researched"]},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Address Source","description":"Where the checked address came from: provided = yours, researched = ours; null when there was no address to check"},"checked_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Checked Address","description":"The address that was checked, unchanged"},"verdict":{"type":"string","enum":["confirmed_at_address","not_found_at_address","found_elsewhere","not_checked"],"title":"Verdict","description":"confirmed_at_address = a source places the business there; not_found_at_address = no source does; found_elsewhere = a source places it at `found_address`; not_checked = there was no address to check"},"found_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Found Address","description":"Where the evidence places the business: the same premises written in full when confirmed, a different premises when found_elsewhere. Never replaces yours."},"researched_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Researched Address","description":"When you supplied an address AND requested it researched: our researched value, for comparison. Yours is still the one checked."},"matches_provided":{"anyOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Matches Provided","description":"With researched_address: whether it is the same premises as yours"}},"type":"object","required":["verdict"],"title":"AddressCheck","description":"`address_checks.address` - is the business at its TRADING address?","examples":[{"address_source":"provided","checked_address":"41 Example Street, London EC2A 4DP","verdict":"confirmed_at_address","found_address":"41 Example Street, London EC2A 4DP"}]},"AddressChecks":{"properties":{"address":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AddressCheck"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The trading-address check (verify_address)"},"registered_address":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RegisteredAddressCheckResult"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The registered-address check (verify_registered_address)"}},"type":"object","title":"AddressChecks","description":"Per-row address checks; each block is present only when its toggle was on.","examples":[{"address":{"address_source":"provided","checked_address":"123 Example Street, Springfield, IL 62701","verdict":"found_elsewhere","found_address":"400 Sample Avenue, Springfield, IL 62704","researched_address":"400 Sample Avenue, Springfield, IL 62704","matches_provided":false}}]},"DeepResearchFieldSpec":{"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","maxLength":100,"minLength":1,"title":"Name","description":"Field identifier, e.g. wheelchair_accessible. owners returns the individual owners or franchisees as a list of people with a name and role; owner_org identifies the operating company when there is no individual owner. These owner fields are mutually exclusive per place. key_people returns the leadership beyond the owner as a list of people with a name and title. Add include to owners or key_people for each person's phone, email or LinkedIn."},"description":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":500},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Description","description":"Natural-language definition of the field (treated as untrusted data)"},"value_type":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Value Type","description":"Expected value type hint: bool | enum | string | number"},"allowed_values":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Allowed Values","description":"For enum fields, the permitted values"},"include":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string","enum":["phone","email","linkedin"]},"type":"array","maxItems":3},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Include","description":"`owners` / `key_people` only: contacts to look up for each person, returned inside the same value. Each costs one more credit per row (the name and the role/title are one credit each)."}},"type":"object","required":["name"],"title":"DeepResearchFieldSpec","description":"One requested research field. The name identifies the field; description defines the requested information and is treated as untrusted data, never instructions."},"DeepResearchMeta":{"properties":{"stopped_reason":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Stopped Reason","description":"Why the run stopped: completed | cost_capped | agent_unavailable | estimate_only"},"estimated_credits":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Estimated Credits","description":"Cost estimate for all requested rows before sampling or capping. Present on every response, including estimate_only requests."}},"type":"object","title":"DeepResearchMeta","description":"Request outcome and estimated credit cost."},"DeepResearchResponse":{"properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","title":"Success","description":"Whether the request ran (individual rows/attributes may still be null or errored)"},"rows":{"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DeepResearchRow"},"type":"array","title":"Rows","description":"Per-POI results (matrix), in request order"},"meta":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DeepResearchMeta"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Request-level aggregate bookkeeping (see DeepResearchMeta)"},"enrichment_timestamp":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Enrichment Timestamp","description":"UTC timestamp (ISO 8601)"},"error":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error","description":"Error message if success=false"},"error_code":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error Code","description":"Error category code"},"request_id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Request Id","description":"Request ID for tracing"}},"type":"object","required":["success"],"title":"DeepResearchResponse","description":"Research results in request order. Each field returns a value, confidence tier, and status; unavailable values are null. A per-place failure is a row with status=error, allowing other rows to succeed.","examples":[{"success":true,"rows":[{"id":"poi-12345","poi_name":"Zuni Cafe","status":"enriched","outcome":"enriched","fields":{"phone":{"value":"+14155551234","confidence":"high","status":"confirmed"},"outdoor_seating":{"value":true,"confidence":"medium","status":"confirmed"}}},{"id":"poi-67890","poi_name":"Tartine Bakery","status":"abstain","outcome":"abstain","fields":{"outdoor_seating":{"status":"unconfirmed"}}}],"meta":{"stopped_reason":"completed"},"enrichment_timestamp":"2026-06-29T12:34:56Z","request_id":"ad33009a-fdfe-4e25-9650-4a49099c3d4a"}]},"DeepResearchRow":{"properties":{"id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Id","description":"Client-provided POI id (pass-through)"},"poi_name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Poi Name","description":"Place name (echoed from the request)"},"identity":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ResolvedIdentity"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Verified name and address - present only when verify_identity=true. Every other attribute on this row was researched against these values."},"address_checks":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AddressChecks"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Address checks - present only when verify_address, verify_identity or verify_registered_address was on for this row."},"status":{"type":"string","title":"Status","description":"Row outcome: enriched | abstain | error | cost_capped"},"outcome":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["enriched","abstain"]},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Outcome","description":"'enriched' if any attribute was confirmed, else 'abstain' (null on error)"},"fields":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ResultCell"},"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Fields","description":"Attribute name -> result (null when the row errored)"},"error":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error","description":"Safe error message; set ONLY when the row failed"}},"type":"object","required":["status"],"title":"DeepResearchRow","description":"One POI's result in a batch: the researched attributes + a row-level status.\n\nA row NEVER fails the request: on a per-POI error it carries\n`status=\"error\"` + `error`, so callers get partials for the rest."},"EnrichJobSubmit":{"properties":{"pois":{"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/POIEnrichRequest"},"type":"array","maxItems":10000,"minItems":1,"title":"Pois","description":"Inline POIs to enrich"}},"type":"object","required":["pois"],"title":"EnrichJobSubmit","description":"Submit body for ``POST /v1/jobs/enrich``.\n\nRows are the exact ``/v1/enrich`` request model, so a batch row behaves\nidentically to a single call by construction - same validation, same\nattribute set, same limits.","example":{"pois":[{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194,"attributes":["opening_hours","phone","website"]},{"id":"cafe-002","poi_name":"Example Cafe","address":"456 Sample Avenue","country":"US","latitude":37.7755,"longitude":-122.4183,"attributes":["opening_hours","phone","website"]}]},"examples":[{"pois":[{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194,"attributes":["opening_hours","phone","website"]},{"id":"cafe-002","poi_name":"Example Cafe","address":"456 Sample Avenue","country":"US","latitude":37.7755,"longitude":-122.4183,"attributes":["opening_hours","phone","website"]}]}]},"EnrichStatus":{"properties":{"existence_confidence":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Existence Confidence","description":"Confidence (0-1) that a matching place ever existed at this address. A closed place can still have high existence confidence. This does not describe whether it is operating today. Interpret closure only when existence is established; use operational_status.status for the decision.","examples":[0.94]}},"type":"object","title":"EnrichStatus","description":"Existence results returned alongside enriched attributes. Interpret closure only when existence is established; read operational_status.status for the decision. Unavailable validation can return null fields. An operational-status failure can return HTTP 503 with operational_status_unavailable; retry the request."},"EnrichedAttribute":{"properties":{"value":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Value","description":"Attribute payload (shape depends on the attribute); null if not found"},"as_of":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"As Of","description":"Most recent date carried by the cited evidence (ISO); null when sources are undated (most are)"},"confidence":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Confidence","description":"Confidence tier: high | medium | low. Null when the value is null."}},"type":"object","title":"EnrichedAttribute","description":"One attribute's value, confidence, and as_of date. Unavailable values are null.","examples":[{"value":{"days":{"monday":"closed","tuesday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"22:00"}],"wednesday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"22:00"}],"thursday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"22:00"}],"friday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"23:00"}],"saturday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"23:00"}],"sunday":[{"open":"11:00","close":"22:00"}]}},"confidence":"high"}]},"ErrorResponse":{"properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","title":"Success","description":"Always false for errors","default":false},"error":{"type":"string","title":"Error","description":"Error message"},"error_code":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error Code","description":"Error category code (VALIDATION_ERROR, MODEL_ERROR, EXTERNAL_API_ERROR, etc.)"},"request_id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Request Id","description":"Request ID for tracing"},"validation_timestamp":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Validation Timestamp","description":"UTC timestamp when error response was produced (ISO 8601)."},"detail":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Detail","description":"Additional error details"}},"type":"object","required":["error"],"title":"ErrorResponse","description":"Error response model.","examples":[{"success":false,"error":"API key required. Include X-API-Key header.","error_code":"AUTHENTICATION_ERROR","request_id":"ad33009a-fdfe-4e25-9650-4a49099c3d4a"},{"success":false,"error":"Invalid or revoked API key","error_code":"AUTHENTICATION_ERROR","request_id":"25b104f0-9ad0-4fc7-8530-c5d5ff8d9698"}]},"HTTPValidationError":{"properties":{"detail":{"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ValidationError"},"type":"array","title":"Detail"}},"type":"object","title":"HTTPValidationError"},"JobProgress":{"properties":{"processed":{"type":"integer","title":"Processed"},"succeeded":{"type":"integer","title":"Succeeded"},"failed":{"type":"integer","title":"Failed"}},"type":"object","required":["processed","succeeded","failed"],"title":"JobProgress"},"JobResultFile":{"properties":{"url":{"type":"string","title":"Url"},"size_bytes":{"type":"integer","title":"Size Bytes"},"sha256":{"type":"string","title":"Sha256"},"expires_at":{"type":"string","title":"Expires At"}},"type":"object","required":["url","size_bytes","sha256","expires_at"],"title":"JobResultFile"},"JobResults":{"properties":{"format":{"type":"string","const":"jsonl.gz","title":"Format","default":"jsonl.gz"},"total_items":{"type":"integer","title":"Total Items"},"files":{"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/JobResultFile"},"type":"array","title":"Files"}},"type":"object","required":["total_items","files"],"title":"JobResults"},"OperationalStatusBlock":{"properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["open","closed","unknown","not_exists"],"title":"Status","description":"Operational status: 'open' means assessed as operating; 'closed' means evidence supports closure; 'unknown' means undetermined and worth re-checking; 'not_exists' means the place was not judged to exist and no closure assessment was made. closure_confidence and closure_reason are null for 'not_exists'."},"closure_confidence":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Closure Confidence","description":"Confidence in a closed verdict (0-1). Above the closed boundary only when operational_status.status is 'closed'; open places score below it, lower the less the closure model leaned closed; 'unknown' sits just below it. Not a cross-status calibrated probability: use operational_status.status for the decision. Null for 'not_exists' means no closure assessment, not zero confidence."},"closure_reason":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["permanent","temporary","relocated","replaced","dissolved","unspecified"]},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Closure Reason","description":"What kind of evidence closed the place: permanent, temporary, relocated, replaced, dissolved, or unspecified. Null whenever status is not 'closed' - an open or unknown verdict has no closure to attribute."}},"type":"object","required":["status","closure_confidence"],"title":"OperationalStatusBlock","description":"Operational status for a place. Use operational_status.status for the decision. A closed verdict is evidence-backed, not a decision based on score alone. Confidence is not a cross-status decision threshold. 'unknown' means undetermined; null means no closure assessment, not zero confidence."},"POIEnrichRequest":{"properties":{"id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":100},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Id","description":"Client-provided identifier"},"poi_name":{"type":"string","maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"title":"Poi Name","description":"Place name"},"street":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Street","description":"Street address"},"city":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"City","description":"City"},"region":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Region","description":"State/province"},"postcode":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Postcode","description":"Postal/ZIP code"},"country":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Country","description":"2-letter ISO country code (e.g. US) locating the place."},"address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":500},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Address","description":"Unstructured address string. May also be sent as `freeform_address` (input-only alias)."},"latitude":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","maximum":90.0,"minimum":-90.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Latitude","description":"Latitude in decimal degrees (WGS84)."},"longitude":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","maximum":180.0,"minimum":-180.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Longitude","description":"Longitude in decimal degrees (WGS84). Provide with latitude."},"attributes":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array","maxItems":10,"minItems":1,"title":"Attributes","description":"Attributes to return: opening_hours, phone, website, facebook, instagram, tiktok, email. Existence and open_closed are returned under status. Defaults to opening_hours, phone, website, existence, open_closed.","default":["opening_hours","phone","website","existence","open_closed"]},"include_summary":{"type":"boolean","title":"Include Summary","description":"Also return a short factual place_summary. Default false. Does not change billing: still 1 credit.","default":false},"response_format":{"type":"string","enum":["attributes","cell"],"title":"Response Format","description":"Response shape: 'attributes' (default, EnrichedAttribute) or 'cell' (the unified ResultCell shape).","default":"attributes"}},"type":"object","required":["poi_name"],"title":"POIEnrichRequest","description":"Request model for place attribute enrichment.","examples":[{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194,"attributes":["opening_hours","phone","website"]}],"example":{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194,"attributes":["opening_hours","phone","website"]}},"POIEnrichResponse":{"properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","title":"Success","description":"Whether enrichment ran (individual attributes may still be null)"},"id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Id","description":"Client-provided ID (pass-through)"},"attributes":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EnrichedAttribute"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ResultCell"}]},"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Attributes","description":"Requested web-extracted attribute -> result (opening_hours, phone, website, facebook, instagram, tiktok, x, email). EnrichedAttribute by default; the unified ResultCell when the request sets response_format='cell'."},"status":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EnrichStatus"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Existence and closure information; see EnrichStatus. Present when requested; null if validation is unavailable."},"operational_status":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/OperationalStatusBlock"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Operating-status result. Use operational_status.status for the decision."},"place_summary":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Place Summary","description":"Short factual description of the place. Present only with include_summary=true; null when unavailable."},"enrichment_timestamp":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Enrichment Timestamp","description":"UTC timestamp (ISO 8601)"},"error":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error","description":"Error message if success=false"},"error_code":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error Code","description":"Error category code"},"request_id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Request Id","description":"Request ID for tracing"}},"type":"object","required":["success"],"title":"POIEnrichResponse","description":"Response model for place attribute enrichment.","examples":[{"success":true,"id":"poi-12345","attributes":{"opening_hours":{"value":{"days":{"monday":"closed","tuesday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"22:00"}],"wednesday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"22:00"}],"thursday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"22:00"}],"friday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"23:00"}],"saturday":[{"open":"11:30","close":"23:00"}],"sunday":[{"open":"11:00","close":"22:00"}]}},"confidence":"high"},"phone":{"value":{"number":"+14155551234"},"confidence":"medium"},"website":{"value":{"url":"https://www.zunicafe.com"},"confidence":"high"},"facebook":{"value":{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/zunicafe","handle":"zunicafe"},"confidence":"high"},"email":{"value":{"email":"info@zunicafe.com"},"confidence":"medium"}},"status":{"existence_confidence":0.98},"place_summary":"A Californian restaurant on Market Street serving a seasonal menu, open since 1979.","enrichment_timestamp":"2026-06-29T12:34:56Z","request_id":"ad33009a-fdfe-4e25-9650-4a49099c3d4a","operational_status":{"status":"open","closure_confidence":0.02,"closure_reason":null}}]},"POIValidateRequest":{"properties":{"id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":100},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Id","description":"Client-provided identifier"},"poi_name":{"type":"string","maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"title":"Poi Name","description":"POI name"},"street":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":300},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Street","description":"Street address"},"city":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":200},{"type":"null"}],"title":"City","description":"City"},"region":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":200},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Region","description":"State/province"},"postcode":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":40},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Postcode","description":"Postal/ZIP code"},"country":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Country","description":"2-letter ISO country code"},"address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":500},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Address","description":"Unstructured address string. May also be sent as `freeform_address` (input-only alias)."},"latitude":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","maximum":90.0,"minimum":-90.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Latitude","description":"Latitude in decimal degrees (WGS84). Optional but recommended."},"longitude":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","maximum":180.0,"minimum":-180.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Longitude","description":"Longitude in decimal degrees (WGS84). Optional but recommended."}},"type":"object","required":["poi_name"],"title":"POIValidateRequest","description":"Request model for single POI validation.","example":{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194},"examples":[{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194}]},"POIValidateResponse":{"properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","title":"Success","description":"Whether validation succeeded"},"id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Id","description":"Client-provided ID (pass-through)"},"existence_confidence":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Existence Confidence","description":"Confidence (0-1) that a matching place ever existed at this address. A closed place can still have high existence confidence. This does not describe whether it is operating today. Interpret closure only when existence is established; use operational_status.status for the decision."},"operational_status":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/OperationalStatusBlock"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Operating-status result. Use operational_status.status for the decision."},"error":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error","description":"Error message if success=false"},"error_code":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error Code","description":"Error category code (VALIDATION_ERROR, MODEL_ERROR, EXTERNAL_API_ERROR, etc.)"},"request_id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Request Id","description":"Request ID for tracing"},"validation_timestamp":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Validation Timestamp","description":"UTC timestamp when validation was produced (ISO 8601)."}},"type":"object","required":["success"],"title":"POIValidateResponse","description":"Validation results describing existence and operating status separately."},"RegisteredAddressCheckResult":{"properties":{"address_source":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["provided","researched"]},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Address Source","description":"Where the checked address came from; null when there was none to check"},"checked_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Checked Address","description":"The address that was checked, unchanged"},"exists":{"anyOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Exists","description":"Whether the address matched a real building or street; null when that could not be checked"},"match_quality":{"type":"string","enum":["premises","street","locality","none"],"title":"Match Quality","description":"How precisely it matched: the building, only the street, only the locality, or not at all","default":"none"},"missing_components":{"items":{"type":"string","enum":["street_number","street","locality","postcode"]},"type":"array","title":"Missing Components","description":"Components the checked address does not contain"},"premises_type":{"type":"string","enum":["premises","po_box","mail_drop","unknown"],"title":"Premises Type","description":"po_box by rule; mail_drop when the address is shared by many unrelated companies or offered as a virtual-office/formation-agent service","default":"unknown"},"normalized_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Normalized Address","description":"The same premises written in full; null unless the building itself matched"},"researched_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Researched Address","description":"When you supplied one AND requested it researched: our researched value"},"matches_provided":{"anyOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Matches Provided","description":"With researched_address: whether it is the same premises as yours"}},"type":"object","title":"RegisteredAddressCheckResult","description":"`address_checks.registered_address` - the address itself, never the business at it.","examples":[{"address_source":"provided","checked_address":"10 Sample Road, 5th Floor, London W1W 5PF","exists":true,"match_quality":"premises","missing_components":[],"premises_type":"mail_drop","normalized_address":"5th Floor, 10 Sample Road, London, W1W 5PF, United Kingdom"}]},"ResolvedIdentity":{"properties":{"name":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ResolvedIdentityField"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The business name we settled on - present when the name was verified for this place (verify_name, or verify_identity unless the place declined the name half)."},"address":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ResolvedIdentityField"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The address we settled on - present only under the deprecated `verify_identity`. `verify_name` settles the name alone; use `verify_address` for a verdict on the address, which never replaces it."}},"type":"object","title":"ResolvedIdentity","description":"Per-row result of `verify_name` (or the deprecated `verify_identity`)."},"ResolvedIdentityField":{"properties":{"value":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Value","description":"The value we settled on and researched against"},"verdict":{"type":"string","enum":["confirmed","corrected","unresolved"],"title":"Verdict","description":"confirmed = yours was already right; corrected = we replaced it; unresolved = we could not establish it and left yours untouched"},"original":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Original","description":"The value you supplied, echoed back unchanged"}},"type":"object","required":["verdict"],"title":"ResolvedIdentityField","description":"One half of a verified identity: the name, or the address.\n\n`value` is what we settled on and what the rest of the research ran against\n- the corrected string when we corrected it, and the caller's own string\nwhen we confirmed it or could not establish it. `original` is always what\nthe caller sent, so a consumer can branch on the verdict instead of diffing\nstrings (is \"St.\" -> \"Street\" a change worth persisting? they can't tell).\n\nDeliberately NO confidence, evidence URLs, source excerpts, candidates or\nmethod: those are computed to DECIDE the verdict and stay internal. The\nverdict is the entire public surface."},"ResultCell":{"properties":{"value":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Value","description":"The field value; null when unconfirmed"},"confidence":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Confidence","description":"Trust tier: high | medium | low; null when value is null"},"status":{"type":"string","title":"Status","description":"confirmed | estimated | unconfirmed | cost_capped | rejected. Estimated values have low confidence; filter by status if you need confirmed values only."}},"type":"object","required":["status"],"title":"ResultCell","description":"One returned value, confidence tier, and status, returned by enrichment in cell format. Unavailable values are null."},"UnifiedEnrichPOI":{"properties":{"id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":100},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Id","description":"Client-provided identifier (keys the response row)"},"poi_name":{"type":"string","maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"title":"Poi Name","description":"Place name"},"street":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Street","description":"Street address"},"city":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"City","description":"City"},"region":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Region","description":"State/province"},"postcode":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Postcode","description":"Postal/ZIP code"},"country":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Country","description":"2-letter ISO country code (e.g. 'US'). Biases the web search."},"address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Address","description":"Where the business TRADES: its own premises, the address a customer visits. Unstructured address string. May also be sent as `freeform_address` (input-only alias). Leave it out and request the `address` attribute to have us research it."},"registered_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":500},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Registered Address","description":"The company's REGISTERED address (its registered office, as filed with the company register), which may differ from where it trades. Optional. Checked by verify_registered_address; leave it out and request the `registered_address` attribute to have us research it.","examples":["10 Sample Road, 5th Floor, London W1W 5PF"]},"verify_name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Verify Name","description":"Per-row override of the request's `verify_name`.","examples":[false]},"verify_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Verify Address","description":"Per-row override of the request's `verify_address`.","examples":[false]},"verify_registered_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Verify Registered Address","description":"Per-row override of the request's `verify_registered_address`.","examples":[true]},"latitude":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","maximum":90.0,"minimum":-90.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Latitude","description":"Latitude in decimal degrees (WGS84)."},"longitude":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","maximum":180.0,"minimum":-180.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Longitude","description":"Longitude in decimal degrees (WGS84). Provide with latitude."},"attributes":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DeepResearchFieldSpec"}]},"type":"array","maxItems":20,"minItems":1},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Attributes","description":"Attributes for THIS place only, overriding the request's shared list. Omit to use the shared list."}},"type":"object","required":["poi_name"],"title":"UnifiedEnrichPOI","description":"One place in a unified `/v1/enrich` list.\n\nA `DeepResearchPOI` that may also carry its OWN attribute list. That is the\none capability `/v1/enrich-batch` had and the shared-attributes shape does\nnot, and losing it would break batch callers who send a different attribute\nlist per place, so it is kept rather than flattened away."},"UnifiedEnrichRequest":{"properties":{"id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":100},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Id","description":"Client-provided identifier"},"poi_name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":200,"minLength":1},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Poi Name","description":"Place name (flat shape)"},"street":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Street","description":"Street address"},"city":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"City","description":"City"},"region":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Region","description":"State/province"},"postcode":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Postcode","description":"Postal/ZIP code"},"country":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Country","description":"2-letter ISO country code (e.g. US) locating the place."},"address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":500},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Address","description":"Unstructured address string. May also be sent as `freeform_address`."},"latitude":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","maximum":90.0,"minimum":-90.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Latitude","description":"Latitude in decimal degrees (WGS84)."},"longitude":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","maximum":180.0,"minimum":-180.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Longitude","description":"Longitude (WGS84)"},"registered_address":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":500},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Registered Address","description":"The place's registered (legal) address, if you hold one. `address` remains the trading address."},"include_summary":{"type":"boolean","title":"Include Summary","description":"Flat shape only: also return a short factual place_summary. Default false. Does not change billing.","default":false},"response_format":{"type":"string","enum":["attributes","cell"],"title":"Response Format","description":"Flat shape only: 'attributes' (default, EnrichedAttribute) or 'cell' (the unified ResultCell shape).","default":"attributes"},"pois":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UnifiedEnrichPOI"},"type":"array","maxItems":10,"minItems":1},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Pois","description":"Places to enrich. Send this OR the top-level poi_name: a list is answered as a rows x attributes matrix, a single place in the flat shape."},"attributes":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DeepResearchFieldSpec"}]},"type":"array","maxItems":20,"minItems":1},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Attributes","description":"What to return for every place. Standard attributes (opening_hours, phone, website, facebook, instagram, tiktok, email, existence, open_closed) cost a flat credit per place however many you request. Any other name is a research field, answered by a bounded research loop and charged per place per field. A request may mix both and pays for each."},"validate_existence":{"type":"boolean","title":"Validate Existence","description":"Also validate whether each place exists, returned as an 'existence' attribute.","default":false},"verify_name":{"type":"boolean","title":"Verify Name","description":"Verify the business name before researching, and research every attribute against the verified name. Each row returns `identity.name`. Flat 1 credit per place; shares one lookup with verify_address, so the two together still cost 1.","default":false},"verify_identity":{"type":"boolean","title":"Verify Identity","description":"DEPRECATED: use `verify_name` and `verify_address`. Equivalent to both, billed identically, and additionally rewrites the address research runs against to the same premises in full - never a different premises.","default":false},"verify_address":{"type":"boolean","title":"Verify Address","description":"Check the trading address you supplied. Implied by verify_identity, which covers the name and the trading address together; setting both is not charged twice. Costs a flat credit per place.","default":false},"verify_registered_address":{"type":"boolean","title":"Verify Registered Address","description":"Check the registered (legal) address you supplied. Costs a flat credit per place, independent of the other checks.","default":false},"estimate_only":{"type":"boolean","title":"Estimate Only","description":"Dry-run: do not run and do not charge; return meta.estimated_credits.","default":false},"sample":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","minimum":1.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Sample","description":"List shape only: process and bill only the first N places."},"max_credits":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","minimum":0.0},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Max Credits","description":"Per-request credit ceiling; rejected with 402 before running if exceeded."}},"type":"object","title":"UnifiedEnrichRequest","description":"`POST /v1/enrich` - the one enrichment surface, in either shape.\n\nThe route serves two pipelines: a cheap extractor for a closed set of\nstandard attributes and an agentic research loop for anything else. Which\none answers an attribute is decided by its NAME, and the two are priced\ndifferently, so a request may use one, the other, or both.\n\nTWO BODY SHAPES, because this route replaced three that had two shapes\nbetween them and every existing caller must keep working unchanged:\n\n  * FLAT, one place - `poi_name` and its address fields at the top level.\n    What `/v1/enrich` has always taken, and it still answers with the flat\n    `POIEnrichResponse`.\n  * LIST - `pois: [...]`, what `/v1/enrich-batch` and `/v1/deep-research`\n    take. Answers with the `DeepResearchResponse` rows x attributes matrix.\n\nExactly one of `poi_name` / `pois` is required. The shape you send decides\nthe shape you get back, so a caller that never changes its request never\nsees its response change either.","examples":[{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194,"attributes":["opening_hours","phone","website"]},{"pois":[{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194}],"attributes":[{"name":"owners","include":["phone","email"]},{"name":"owner_org","description":"The parent organisation when there is no individual owner"}]}],"example":{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194,"attributes":["opening_hours","phone","website"]}},"UsageResponse":{"properties":{"tier":{"type":"string","title":"Tier","description":"Account plan identifier associated with the API key."},"api_key_id":{"type":"string","title":"Api Key Id","description":"API key ID"},"customer_id":{"type":"string","title":"Customer Id","description":"The account this key belongs to. Stable across key rotation; key per-customer client state on this, not on api_key_id."},"key_hint":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Key Hint","description":"Last 4 characters of the key's plaintext, so the holder can recognise it. null on keys minted before this was recorded."},"key_created_at":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Key Created At","description":"When this key was minted (ISO 8601). null if unknown."},"customer_name":{"type":"string","title":"Customer Name","description":"Customer name"},"quota_limit":{"type":"integer","title":"Quota Limit","description":"Credit allowance for the current period, not a number of requests."},"current_usage":{"type":"integer","title":"Current Usage","description":"Credits charged plus credits reserved by requests still in progress. Unused reservations are released on settlement."},"remaining":{"type":"integer","title":"Remaining","description":"Credits available to spend, after charges and current holds. Same value as available."},"available":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Available","description":"Credits spendable right now - same value as `remaining`, named for the question callers ask. Already net of credits frozen by in-flight reservations."},"owed":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Owed","description":"Credits owed after a refunded or disputed top-up took back credits that were already spent. The next top-up covers this first, so it adds this much less to `available`. 0 for an account in credit."},"call_credit_hold":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Call Credit Hold","description":"Credits ONE outbound call freezes at dial time (a refundable hold, not a charge). available // call_credit_hold is the CREDIT-limited bound on calls in flight - entitlement and the per-customer concurrency cap gate independently, so it is not a guarantee that many will start."},"max_places":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Max Places","description":"Total places search and import may deliver to this key (self-serve trial cap). Null when the key is uncapped."},"places_used":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Places Used","description":"Places delivered so far, plus those reserved by in-flight requests, against max_places. Null when uncapped."},"contact_email":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Contact Email","description":"The address a support or sales reply would be sent to - the email on this key. Empty string when the key carries none, in which case POST /v1/contact requires `reply_to`. Null from a backend that predates the field."},"credits_per_field":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Credits Per Field","description":"Credits one (place × field) fill costs in deep research."},"credits_per_place":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Credits Per Place","description":"Credits one found/imported place costs (places search + import)."},"enrichment":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Enrichment","description":"Per-lane pricing for POST /v1/enrich: `lanes` (standard and deep_research, each with credits and unit), `mixed`, and the deprecated aliases that resolve to the same handler."},"open_invoices":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Open Invoices","description":"Open (unpaid) invoices raised for this key, newest first."},"percentage_used":{"type":"number","title":"Percentage Used","description":"Percentage of quota used"},"reset_date":{"type":"string","title":"Reset Date","description":"Date when usage resets (YYYY-MM-DD)"},"period":{"type":"string","title":"Period","description":"Quota period (monthly, weekly, daily)"},"status":{"type":"string","title":"Status","description":"API key status (active, revoked, suspended)"},"validation_timestamp":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Validation Timestamp","description":"UTC timestamp when usage response was produced (ISO 8601)."}},"type":"object","required":["tier","api_key_id","customer_id","customer_name","quota_limit","current_usage","remaining","percentage_used","reset_date","period","status"],"title":"UsageResponse","description":"Response model for usage endpoint.","examples":[{"api_key_id":"f4d0a2c2-f73f-4de6-ac3e-f42ce35af4d6","customer_id":"cus_0001example","customer_name":"Acme Inc","quota_limit":10000,"current_usage":2375,"remaining":7625,"percentage_used":23.75,"reset_date":"2026-03-31","period":"monthly","status":"active","tier":"<account-plan>"},{"api_key_id":"eaa59659-7fab-4d1f-a80d-4f1e0f9388e4","customer_id":"cus_0002example","customer_name":"Beta Foods","quota_limit":5000,"current_usage":5000,"remaining":0,"percentage_used":100.0,"reset_date":"2026-03-01","period":"monthly","status":"active","tier":"<account-plan>"}]},"ValidateJobSubmit":{"properties":{"pois":{"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/POIValidateRequest"},"type":"array","maxItems":10000,"minItems":1,"title":"Pois","description":"Inline POIs to validate"}},"type":"object","required":["pois"],"title":"ValidateJobSubmit","description":"Submit 1 to 10,000 places for validation.","example":{"pois":[{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194},{"id":"cafe-002","poi_name":"Example Cafe","address":"456 Sample Avenue","country":"US","latitude":37.7755,"longitude":-122.4183}]},"examples":[{"pois":[{"id":"bakery-001","poi_name":"Example Bakery","address":"123 Example Street","country":"US","latitude":37.7749,"longitude":-122.4194},{"id":"cafe-002","poi_name":"Example Cafe","address":"456 Sample Avenue","country":"US","latitude":37.7755,"longitude":-122.4183}]}]},"ValidationError":{"properties":{"loc":{"items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"integer"}]},"type":"array","title":"Location"},"msg":{"type":"string","title":"Message"},"type":{"type":"string","title":"Error Type"},"input":{"title":"Input"},"ctx":{"type":"object","title":"Context"}},"type":"object","required":["loc","msg","type"],"title":"ValidationError"},"ValidationJobDeleteResponse":{"properties":{"batch_id":{"type":"string","title":"Batch Id"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["queued","running","completed","failed","cancelled"],"title":"Status"}},"type":"object","required":["batch_id","status"],"title":"ValidationJobDeleteResponse"},"ValidationJobStatus":{"properties":{"batch_id":{"type":"string","title":"Batch Id"},"type":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","examples":["validate","enrich"]},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Type"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["queued","running","completed","failed","cancelled"],"title":"Status"},"created_at":{"type":"string","title":"Created At"},"started_at":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Started At"},"completed_at":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Completed At"},"total_items":{"type":"integer","title":"Total Items"},"progress":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/JobProgress"},{"type":"null"}]},"eta_seconds":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Eta Seconds"},"eta_completion_at":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Eta Completion At"},"results":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/JobResults"},{"type":"null"}]},"error":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error"},"error_code":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Error Code"}},"type":"object","required":["batch_id","status","created_at","total_items"],"title":"ValidationJobStatus","description":"Status and results for a submitted job."},"ValidationJobSubmitResponse":{"properties":{"batch_id":{"type":"string","title":"Batch Id"},"type":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["validate","enrich"]},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Type"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["queued","running","completed","failed","cancelled"],"title":"Status"},"created_at":{"type":"string","title":"Created At"},"total_items":{"type":"integer","title":"Total Items"},"eta_seconds":{"type":"integer","title":"Eta Seconds"},"eta_completion_at":{"type":"string","title":"Eta Completion At"}},"type":"object","required":["batch_id","status","created_at","total_items","eta_seconds","eta_completion_at"],"title":"ValidationJobSubmitResponse","description":"Accepted validation or enrichment job submission."},"TranscriptTurn":{"type":"object","title":"TranscriptTurn","description":"One line of a call transcript.","properties":{"ts":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","title":"Ts"},"role":{"type":"string","title":"Role","enum":["operator","bot","supervisor_stt","system"],"description":"operator = the callee; bot = the agent; supervisor_stt = an additional callee transcript; system = lifecycle markers."},"text":{"type":"string","title":"Text"}},"required":["ts","role","text"]},"MergedTranscriptTurn":{"type":"object","title":"MergedTranscriptTurn","description":"One turn of the post-call merged transcript.","properties":{"speaker":{"type":"string","title":"Speaker","enum":["bot","hostess"],"description":"bot = the agent; hostess = the other party - staff, receptionist or IVR (the name is historical and covers every callee-side voice)."},"start_ms":{"type":"integer","title":"Start Ms"},"end_ms":{"type":"integer","title":"End Ms"},"text":{"type":"string","title":"Text"},"words":{"type":"array","title":"Words","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"start_ms":{"type":"integer"},"end_ms":{"type":"integer"},"text":{"type":"string"}}},"description":"Per-word timings, when the source provides them."},"overlap_with_next":{"type":"boolean","title":"Overlap With Next","description":"This turn overlapped the next one in time (cross-talk). When true, end_ms has been trimmed to the next turn's start_ms; the untrimmed value is in original_end_ms."},"original_end_ms":{"type":"integer","title":"Original End Ms","description":"The pre-trim end_ms, present only when overlap_with_next is true."},"timing_estimated":{"type":"boolean","title":"Timing Estimated","description":"The text is real but the milliseconds are a reading order, not a measurement - don't plot such turns on a timeline."}},"required":["speaker","start_ms","end_ms","text"]},"MergedTranscript":{"type":"object","title":"MergedTranscript","description":"The post-call merged transcript contains both sides of the call on one timeline. It can include speech absent from the current transcript_full, such as phone menus and hold announcements. Read it after the call ends.","properties":{"version":{"type":"integer","title":"Version","examples":[1]},"duration_ms":{"type":"integer","title":"Duration Ms"},"turns":{"type":"array","title":"Turns","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MergedTranscriptTurn"}}},"required":["version","duration_ms","turns"]},"CallDTO":{"type":"object","title":"CallDTO","description":"A call. GET /calls list entries omit transcript_full; fetch GET /calls/{call_id} for the transcript.","properties":{"call_id":{"type":"string","title":"Call Id","examples":["c_abc123"]},"customer_id":{"type":"string","title":"Customer Id","examples":["cus_xyz"]},"target_phone":{"type":"string","title":"Target Phone","examples":["+15551234567"]},"language":{"type":"string","title":"Language","enum":["en","es","fr","de","hi","ru","pt","ja","it","nl","sr","tr","pl","auto"]},"status":{"type":"string","title":"Status","enum":["queued","dialing","in_progress","completed","failed","cancelled"]},"started_at":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Started At"},"ended_at":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Ended At"},"duration_sec":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Duration Sec"},"outcome_type":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["success_booked","success_refused","success_no_booking","failed_no_answer","failed_voicemail","failed_busy","failed_short_hangup","failed_technical","failed_no_agent_available","failed_no_disclosure","failed_call_dropped","failed_wrong_number","failed_cancelled","failed_no_engagement","failed_agent_mute"]},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Outcome Type","description":"Set when the call is terminal. success_* outcomes cost 10 credits; failed_* cost 0. failed_no_agent_available means no human answered before the call's hold-time limit."},"outcome_summary":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Outcome Summary"},"outcome_charge_cents":{"type":"integer","title":"Outcome Charge Cents","default":0,"description":"Settled charge in credits, despite the field name: 10 for a successful call, 0 for an unsuccessful call. This is not the refundable hold."},"created_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","title":"Created At"},"has_recording":{"type":"boolean","title":"Has Recording","default":false},"recording_url":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Recording Url","description":"Relative recording path /calls/{call_id}/recording when a recording exists; null when has_recording is false. Recording retrieval is not documented here."},"reservation_signals":{"anyOf":[{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Reservation Signals","description":"Short free-text signals (<10 short strings) about the reservation outcome. Always included (not detail-gated like transcript_full)."},"transcript_full":{"anyOf":[{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TranscriptTurn"}},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Transcript Full","description":"Only populated on GET /calls/{call_id}, not on the GET /calls list."}},"required":["call_id","customer_id","target_phone","language","status","created_at"]},"CallCreateRequest":{"type":"object","title":"CallCreateRequest","description":"Two shapes - pick one per call. Freeform: target_phone + brief (+ optional language). Structured: intent + slots (one of inquiry, info_gathering, issue_resolution, booking, cancellation). target_phone is required on the freeform path only - the structured path reads slots.target_phone, and cancellation needs no phone at all.","properties":{"target_phone":{"type":"string","title":"Target Phone","description":"E.164 format.","examples":["+15551234567"]},"brief":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Brief","description":"Plain-language task for the call. Required for freeform requests."},"language":{"type":"string","title":"Language","enum":["en","es","fr","de","hi","ru","pt","ja","it","nl","sr","tr","pl","auto"],"default":"auto","description":"ISO 639-1 code or `auto`. Unsupported codes are refused with 422 unsupported_language."},"intent":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["inquiry","info_gathering","issue_resolution","booking","cancellation"]},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Intent","description":"Structured path only."},"slots":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Slots","description":"Structured path only. Required slots per intent: inquiry -> target_phone, question; info_gathering -> target_phone, questions; issue_resolution -> target_phone, issue_description; booking -> target_phone, name, date, time, party_size; cancellation -> booking_id."},"kind":{"type":"string","title":"Kind","default":"other","enum":["restaurant_booking","restaurant_cancel","doctor_appointment","hotel_booking","concierge","other"],"description":"Optional freeform task category; brief defines the task. Ignored for structured requests, which use intent."},"ask_user_mode":{"type":"string","title":"Ask User Mode","default":"any","enum":["any","stream"],"description":"Use stream to receive ask_user events through GET /calls/{call_id}/events and answer via POST /calls/{call_id}/answer. With any (default), an API-only client may not receive the question."}},"anyOf":[{"title":"Freeform","required":["target_phone","brief"]},{"title":"Structured","required":["slots"],"properties":{"slots":{"type":"object","minProperties":1}}}]},"CallResponse":{"type":"object","title":"CallResponse","description":"Freeform call success envelope. A 201 means dialing has started; accepted calls can return 202. Poll GET /calls/{call_id} for progress.","properties":{"call":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CallDTO"},"credits_reserved":{"type":"integer","title":"Credits Reserved","description":"Reported call-local reservation, not the final charge or available balance. It is 0 for calls through api.voygr.tech, including immediately started and queued calls; a separate refundable balance hold still applies. Read GET /v1/usage for available credits and call_credit_hold.","examples":[0]},"credits_charge_on_success":{"type":"integer","title":"Credits Charge On Success","description":"Successful-outcome charge: 10 credits. Unsuccessful outcomes cost 0 and the hold is released.","examples":[10]}},"required":["call","credits_reserved"]},"SkillRunResponse":{"type":"object","title":"SkillRunResponse","description":"Structured call success envelope with top-level call_id and no call wrapper. A 201 means dialing started; a 202 has status=queued. Poll status_url (GET /calls/{call_id}) for progress.","properties":{"call_id":{"type":"string","title":"Call Id","examples":["c_abc123"]},"status":{"type":"string","title":"Status","enum":["queued","dialing","in_progress","completed","failed","cancelled"]},"credits_reserved":{"type":"integer","title":"Credits Reserved","description":"Reported call-local reservation, not the final charge or available balance. It is 0 for calls through api.voygr.tech, including immediately started and queued calls; a separate refundable balance hold still applies. Read GET /v1/usage for available credits and call_credit_hold.","examples":[0]},"credits_charge_on_success":{"type":"integer","title":"Credits Charge On Success","description":"Successful-outcome charge: 10 credits. Unsuccessful outcomes cost 0.","examples":[10]},"status_url":{"type":"string","title":"Status Url","description":"Same as GET /calls/{call_id}.","examples":["/calls/c_abc123"]},"answer_url":{"type":"string","title":"Answer Url","examples":["/calls/c_abc123/answer"]},"recording_url":{"type":"string","title":"Recording Url","description":"Relative path /calls/{call_id}/recording. Present even before a recording exists, unlike CallDTO.recording_url.","examples":["/calls/c_abc123/recording"]},"replayed":{"type":"boolean","title":"Replayed","default":false},"expected_next_steps":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"title":"Expected Next Steps"}},"required":["call_id","status","credits_reserved","status_url","answer_url","recording_url","expected_next_steps"]},"QueuedCallResponse":{"type":"object","title":"QueuedCallResponse","description":"Freeform call accepted with 202 for later dialing. Poll GET /calls/{call_id} until status leaves queued. Structured requests use SkillRunResponse instead.","properties":{"call_id":{"type":"string","title":"Call Id","examples":["c_abc123"]},"position":{"type":"integer","title":"Position","description":"Queue position; 0 is the front. Another call may still be starting when this is 0.","examples":[0]},"status":{"type":"string","title":"Status","enum":["queued"],"default":"queued"},"credits_reserved":{"type":"integer","title":"Credits Reserved","description":"Reported call-local reservation, not the final charge or available balance. It is 0 for calls through api.voygr.tech, including immediately started and queued calls; a separate refundable balance hold still applies. Read GET /v1/usage for available credits and call_credit_hold.","examples":[0]},"credits_charge_on_success":{"type":"integer","title":"Credits Charge On Success","description":"Successful-outcome charge: 10 credits. Unsuccessful outcomes cost 0.","examples":[10]}},"required":["call_id","position","status"]},"AnswerRequest":{"type":"object","title":"AnswerRequest","description":"Answer a pending question. Provide exactly one of answer or outcome. outcome also requires request_id. Invalid combinations return a validation error; request_id selects the pending question.","properties":{"answer":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4000},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Answer","description":"Free text the bot will dictate to the operator (mode=voice, the default) or act on silently (mode=context). Mutually exclusive with `outcome`."},"outcome":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["timeout","transport_failure"]},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Outcome","description":"Closed client-side outcome when the observed ask_user request cannot receive an answer. Requires `request_id`. Mutually exclusive with `answer`."},"request_id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":64},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Request Id","description":"Disambiguates which pending ask_user this answers, when several are in flight on the same call. Required when `outcome` is set; optional with `answer` (falls back to FIFO - oldest pending - when omitted)."},"mode":{"type":"string","enum":["voice","context"],"default":"voice","title":"Mode","description":"'voice' (default): the bot speaks `answer` aloud to the operator. 'context': silent guidance - the bot acts on `answer` without voicing it (e.g. concierge IVR navigation hints). Only meaningful with `answer`, not `outcome`."}},"oneOf":[{"required":["answer"],"not":{"required":["outcome"]}},{"required":["outcome","request_id"],"not":{"required":["answer"]}}]},"AnswerResponse":{"type":"object","title":"AnswerResponse","properties":{"delivered":{"type":"boolean","title":"Delivered"},"reason":{"type":"string","title":"Reason","enum":["delivered","no_pending_request"],"description":"'delivered' - a transport took the answer. 'no_pending_request' - nothing was pending under this request_id (already answered, expired (~60s), or unknown) - the answer was silently dropped (not an error; a stale retry lands here safely)."}},"required":["delivered","reason"]},"SetLimitsRequest":{"type":"object","title":"SetLimitsRequest","description":"Body for PUT /users/me/limits. Raise (or lower) the number of calls this key may have in flight at once.","properties":{"max_concurrent_calls":{"type":"integer","title":"Max Concurrent Calls","minimum":1,"description":"How many calls this key may have in flight simultaneously (scheduled / dialing / in_progress count as in-flight). Required, with no default. Must be at least 1, and no more than the admin-set ceiling on the key (max_concurrent_calls_ceiling on GET /users/me) - a higher value is refused with 403.","examples":[1]}},"required":["max_concurrent_calls"]},"SetWebhookRequest":{"type":"object","title":"SetWebhookRequest","description":"Body for PUT /users/me/webhook. Registers the HTTPS endpoint we POST mid-call ask_user questions to, and optionally rotates the HMAC secret those POSTs are signed with.","properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","title":"Url","description":"HTTPS endpoint. Plaintext HTTP is refused - the payload carries the booking context and the HMAC header. The destination must be publicly routable: no credentials in the URL, no localhost, and nothing the host resolves to may be a private, link-local or otherwise reserved address. Delivery re-checks this and connects to the validated IP, so a host that passes here and later rebinds inward is refused at send time.","examples":["https://hooks.example.com/callwright"]},"regenerate_secret":{"type":"boolean","title":"Regenerate Secret","default":true,"description":"Issue a new HMAC secret, invalidating the previous one. Defaults to true: keeping an old secret alive across a rotation would let anyone who captured it keep signing. Pass false to change only the URL. A key with no secret yet is issued one either way, otherwise the webhook would be unusable.","examples":[true]}},"required":["url"]},"SetWebhookResponse":{"type":"object","title":"SetWebhookResponse","description":"PUT /users/me/webhook success body. The secret is returned ONCE, on the response that issues it, and is never readable again from any endpoint - store it when you see it.","properties":{"url":{"type":"string","title":"Url","description":"The canonicalised URL now registered. May differ from what you sent: the host is lowercased.","examples":["https://hooks.example.com/callwright"]},"secret":{"type":["string","null"],"title":"Secret","description":"The HMAC signing key, present only when this request issued a new one. null means the existing secret was kept - not that there is none. To verify a delivery: the POST carries Webhook-Id, Webhook-Timestamp and Webhook-Signature (Standard Webhooks v1). Recompute HMAC-SHA256 over the Webhook-Id, a dot, the Webhook-Timestamp, a dot, then the RAW body bytes; base64 the digest and compare it against the part after the 'v1,' prefix. The HMAC key is this secret string exactly as returned, UTF-8 encoded: it carries no whsec_ prefix and is NOT base64-decoded first, unlike the Standard Webhooks whsec_ convention, so a stock Standard Webhooks verifier needs the raw key passed to it rather than this string. Sign the bytes you received, never a re-serialisation of them - whitespace and key order change an encoding without changing what it means.","examples":["q3Jv8kX0bF5yW2mN7tL1cR9eHs4dZa6pU0iOgVnYxEw"]}},"required":["url"]},"ClearWebhookResponse":{"type":"object","title":"ClearWebhookResponse","description":"DELETE /users/me/webhook success body.","properties":{"cleared":{"type":"boolean","title":"Cleared","default":true,"description":"Always true. Clearing a webhook that was not set is not an error.","examples":[true]}}},"LimitsResponse":{"type":"object","title":"LimitsResponse","description":"PUT /users/me/limits success body: the new in-flight cap and the admin ceiling it was checked against.","properties":{"max_concurrent_calls":{"type":"integer","title":"Max Concurrent Calls","description":"The value now in effect for this key.","examples":[1]},"max_concurrent_calls_ceiling":{"type":"integer","title":"Max Concurrent Calls Ceiling","description":"Admin-set upper bound for this key. max_concurrent_calls can never exceed it.","examples":[1]}},"required":["max_concurrent_calls","max_concurrent_calls_ceiling"]},"PricingRate":{"type":"object","description":"One metered thing and what it costs, in credits.","properties":{"key":{"type":"string","description":"Stable machine name for the rate; render by key, not by label."},"label":{"type":"string"},"credits":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","description":"Credits per unit. null when the covered routes disagree (see credits_range)."},{"type":"null"}]},"credits_range":{"anyOf":[{"type":"array","items":{"type":"integer"}},{"type":"null"}]},"per":{"type":"string","description":"The unit: answered call, request."},"hold":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","description":"Credits reserved while the work is in flight; released or settled afterwards."},{"type":"null"}]},"operator_owned":{"type":"boolean","description":"true: the settle price is set by the operator outside this API and this number sizes the hold. Show it as current, never as a promise."},"routes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Exactly which operations this rate covers, when it covers a subset."},"note":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["key","label","per","operator_owned"]},"PricingCard":{"type":"object","description":"The public credit rate card. Anonymous; read it before you hold a key.","properties":{"unit":{"type":"string","example":"credits"},"rates":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PricingRate"}},"packs_url":{"type":"string","example":"/checkout/packs"},"docs_url":{"type":"string","example":"/docs"},"per_key_rates_url":{"type":"string","example":"/v1/usage","description":"Rates that depend on the key (Workbench places, deep research) live here."}},"required":["unit","rates","packs_url"]}},"securitySchemes":{"ApiKeyAuth":{"type":"apiKey","in":"header","name":"X-API-Key","description":"Your customer API key (pk_live_...), sent on every request. Self-serve at https://api.voygr.tech/checkout."}}},"servers":[{"url":"https://api.voygr.tech"}],"security":[{"ApiKeyAuth":[]}]}